\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Beak, day of God, O break,
\par Sweet light of heavenly skies!
\par I all for thee forsake,
\par And from my dead self rise:
\par O Lamb of God, Whose love is light,
\par Shine on my soul, and all is bright!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Break, day of God, O break !\tab 
\par The night has lingered long;
\par Our hearts with sighing wake,
\par We weep for sin and wrong:
\par O Bright and Morning Star, draw near;
\par O Sun of Righteousness, appear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Break, day of God, O break !
\par The earth with strife is worn ;
\par The hills with thunder shake,
\par Hearts of the people mourn :
\par Break, day of God, sweet day of peace,
\par And bid the shout of warriors cease !
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Break, day of God, O break,
\par Like to the days above !
\par Let purity awake,
\par And faith, and hope ,and love :
\par But lo, we see the brightening sky ;
\par The golden morn is drawing nigh.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

